// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  LITTLE NIGHTMARES — ORIGINAL CHARACTER & WORLD GENERATOR
//  "Every shadow has a story. Every story has a name."
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

generateImage = {import:text-to-image-plugin}
kv = {import:kv-plugin}

// ── META ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
$meta
  title = Little Nightmares OC Generator
  description = Create original characters, locations, and entire game concepts set in the haunting world of Little Nightmares. Generate eerie 2D artwork, backstories, chapters, and endings.
  tags = little nightmares, oc generator, character creator, horror, dark fantasy, game concept
  header
    mode = minimal

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  TONE / DIFFICULTY — from fairy-tale eerie to full horror
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Tone level is set via window.currentToneLevel from the slider JS
getCurrentToneLevel() =>
  if (typeof window !== "undefined" && window.currentToneLevel !== undefined)
    return window.currentToneLevel;
  return 1;

toneLabel
  Fairy-Tale Eerie
  Unsettling
  Dark
  Full Horror

toneDesc
  Fairy-Tale Eerie = Whimsical and melancholic. The dark here is soft, like a bruise beneath the skin of a dream. Dread is suggested, never shown. Children still sing, badly.
  Unsettling = The default register of this place. Atmosphere thick with unease. Things are wrong in ways you cannot quite name.
  Dark = Heavy and oppressive. Decay is visible. The horror is no longer suggested — it is present, patient, and close.
  Full Horror = Visceral and grotesque. No comfort is offered. The place shows its teeth. So do the things in it.

toneImageModifier(level) =>
  if (level === 0) return "Soft painterly fairy-tale illustration style, whimsical but melancholic, Studio Ghibli meets dark fairy tale, muted warm pastel tones, gentle soft shadows, wonder mixed with gentle melancholy, beautiful but sad, no gore, no violence, no blood. ";
  if (level === 1) return "Atmospheric creeping dread, muted desaturated colors, subtle unease, shadows that suggest rather than show, gentle decay, no explicit gore. ";
  if (level === 2) return "Heavy oppressive atmosphere, deep stark shadows, visible decay and ruin, visceral unease, rust rot and grime, body horror suggested, disturbing imagery, claustrophobic. ";
  return "Visceral grotesque horror, explicit dread, distorted flesh and bone, grotesque swollen proportions, blood rust and decay, nightmare imagery, disturbing and visceral, explicit body horror, claustrophobic dread. ";

toneAtmoFairy
  The dark here is soft, like velvet worn thin — something hums a lullaby that was almost kind.
  A moth lands on your hand. It is warm. It stays. The dread is a whisper, not a shout.
  The corridors are vast but lit with a gentle amber, and the shadows bow rather than reach.
  Something watches, but its gaze is curious, not hungry. Not yet.
  The air smells of old paper and dried lavender. The fear is beautiful, if you can call it fear.
  The place is sad, not cruel. It has forgotten why it is the way it is. So have you.
  The wallpaper peels to reveal flowers, not stains. A child laughed here once. You can almost hear it.
  The dark is a blanket, not a mouth. It holds you. It does not swallow. Not yet.

toneAtmoUnsettling
  The air holds its breath. Something is wrong, but it will not show you what. Not yet.
  The silence has a texture — like skin, like waiting. You are being patient. So is it.
  The walls are the wrong color. The doors are the wrong height. You cannot say how. You just know.
  A sound that might be pipes. A sound that might not. You walk faster.
  Everything is almost normal. The "almost" is the worst part.
  The portraits' eyes follow you — or do they? You are not sure. You are not sure you want to be.
  Something shifted in the corner of your eye. When you looked, it had not moved. That is worse.
  The temperature drops by a single degree and stays there. Someone opened a door somewhere. Or something.

toneAtmoDark
  The walls sweat. The floor gives underfoot. Something here has stopped pretending.
  The smell is unmistakable now — iron, rot, and something sweeter beneath. You know what sweet is.
  The shadows have teeth. Not metaphorically. You can see them, just barely, in the corners.
  The Residents no longer ignore you. They have not moved. But they are facing you now.
  The beauty is gone. Only the ruin remains, and the ruin is hungry.
  The pipes groan with something that is not water. The walls are thinner here. They are thin on purpose.
  You find a handprint on the wall. It is smaller than yours. It is still warm.
  The lights dim as you pass. Not all of them come back. You are leaving a trail of dark behind you.

toneAtmoHorror
  The place has opened its mouth. You are inside it. It knows.
  The walls are breathing — wet, ragged, hungry breaths. The floor is warm and yielding and you do not look down.
  Something ahead is making a sound that was once a child's voice. It is not a child's voice anymore.
  The dark here is not absence. It is presence. It has weight. It has intent. It has noticed you.
  Blood on the walls, old and new, layered like wallpaper. The pattern is faces. The faces are moving.
  Something behind you is chewing. It has been chewing for a long time. It is almost done.
  The floor is slick. You do not look down. You know what it is. You can smell it between your toes.
  A Resident stands in the corridor ahead, smiling with too many teeth. It has been waiting for you. It is patient. It is done waiting.

getToneLabel() =>
  let labels = ["Fairy-Tale Eerie", "Unsettling", "Dark", "Full Horror"];
  return labels[getCurrentToneLevel()] || "Unsettling";

getToneAtmosphere() =>
  let level = getCurrentToneLevel();
  if (level === 0) return toneAtmoFairy.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  if (level === 1) return toneAtmoUnsettling.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  if (level === 2) return toneAtmoDark.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  return toneAtmoHorror.selectOne.evaluateItem;


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CHARACTER TYPES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
characterType
  Kid^3
  Resident
  Guest
  Monster
  Wanderer
  Protector
  Runaway
  Stowaway

characterTypeDesc
  Kid = A small, fragile soul navigating a world far too large. Survival is measured in inches and held breath.
  Resident = A permanent denizen of this cursed place — bent, broken, and bound to its routines. They were not always this way.
  Guest = A visitor who came willingly, seduced by promise of feast or refuge. Now they cannot leave. They do not wish to.
  Monster = Something that was perhaps once a person. The hunger has long since consumed whatever remained of kindness.
  Wanderer = They belong to no place and no place wants them. The corridors shift behind them. They walk on regardless.
  Protector = A soul who has chosen to shield someone smaller than themselves. This kindness may be their undoing — or their salvation.
  Runaway = They escaped once. The place does not forgive escape. It sends its long fingers after them, patient and slow.
  Stowaway = Hidden in the walls, in the pipes, in the gaps between floors. They see everything. They are seen by nothing — until they are.

