// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  AGE — expressed evocatively
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ageKid
  barely old enough to walk alone
  six — the age of yellow raincoats and held breath
  nine — old enough to know fear, young enough to outrun it
  small enough to fit through the pipes
  tall enough now to reach the door handle — barely
  a child by any measure, though the place has aged them

ageResident
  ageless — they have always been here
  old beyond counting, bent like a question mark
  middle-aged in a place where time curdles
  young once, long ago — the halls remember a different face
  ancient and slow, moving like furniture given purpose

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  SPECIAL SKILLS / ABILITIES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
skill
  can flatten their body thin enough to slip under doors
  holds light in their hands — a single spark that frightens the dark things
  hears the walls breathe and knows which corridors will shift
  can mimic any voice perfectly — used to lure or to hide
  never makes a sound when they move, not even on glass
  sees in absolute darkness as though it were noon
  can mend broken things with a touch — toys, bones, promises
  carries a key that opens any lock, but each use costs a memory
  breathes so shallowly that the Hunters cannot find them
  can climb any surface like a spider, silent and sure
  splits their shadow — one stays as a decoy while they flee
  understands the language of the pipes and the mice
  can make themselves forgotten — turn a corner and minds slide off them
  carries a music box whose tune puts the Residents to sleep
  their tears become solid — small hard pearls that buy passage
  can walk on the ceiling when no one is watching
  has a pocket that is bigger inside — they have hidden a child in there before
  their reflection moves independently and scouts ahead
  can taste lies — they taste like copper and old rain
  grows lighter or heavier at will — to float or to anchor
  their breath frosts the air, revealing hidden things and hidden doors
  can swallow small objects whole and bring them back up undamaged — a living smuggler's pocket
  speaks the language of moths and can ask them to carry messages or lead them to exits
  their blood glows faintly, enough to read by in absolute darkness, enough to attract the wrong things
  can hold their breath for an impossible length of time — long enough to cross a flooded corridor
  knows the name of every Resident, and speaking a name aloud makes that Resident briefly forget them
  can sharpen any edge to a razor with a single pass of their fingertip — bone, rust, glass
  leaves no heat signature — to anything that hunts by warmth, they simply are not there
  can hear a heartbeat through a wall and tell whose it is, and whether it is afraid
  their touch rusts metal and rots wood — useful for sabotage, dangerous for everything they own
  can fold themselves into a shape that fits any container — a drawer, a box, a boot
  sees the recent past of any room as a fading image — who stood where, who was taken where
  carries a tune that, when hummed backward, undoes a single lock within earshot

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CLOTHING
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
clothingKid
  a yellow raincoat, far too big, sleeves rolled back six times
  a burlap sack with holes cut for arms, tied with twine
  a nightgown stolen from a Guest's wardrobe, hem dragging in the filth
  a patched sailor's suit, salt-stained and stiff
  layers of stolen scarves wound tight against the cold
  a paper-thin hospital gown, backless, printed with faded flowers
  an oversized cook's apron, still smeared with something brown
  a wool coat missing every button, held shut with safety pins
  a dancer's costume, torn and muddy, sequins falling like shed scales
  nothing but rags bound with strips of curtain
  a paper bag over the head with two eye-holes, and a blanket for a cape
  a too-large uniform from a long-dead attendant, name tag still reading "HELLO"
  a sweater knitted from unraveled socks, every color, none matching
  a faded school uniform with a badge from a school that never existed
  a rain slicker of arterial red, so bright it seems to glow in the dim
  a wrap of old curtain velvet, dusty and grand and absurdly heavy
  a shift of bleached linen, stained at the hem with something dark
  a hand-me-down clown costume, the smile painted on the fabric now cracked
  a onesie far too young for them, printed with lambs, the zipper stuck half-down
  a coat of many pockets, every pocket empty, every pocket searched
  a swimsuit and one sock, as if dressed for a beach that does not exist
  a choir robe, hemmed short, the cowl pulled up to hide the face
  a tutu worn over trousers, both filthy, both stubbornly worn
  a towel pinned at the shoulder like a toga, damp and smelling of mildew

clothingResident
  a moth-eaten butler's tailcoat, seams straining
  a housecoat stained with decades of meals
  a uniform of brass buttons and authority, gone green at the cuffs
  an apron of oiled leather, hung with hooks and keys
  a nightdress worn as daywear, suggesting they never truly wake
  a formal gown gone to grey, hem rotted to fringe
  overalls stiff with dried plaster, boots like anchors
  a judge's robe, moth-eaten, the gavel replaced with a meat tenderizer
  a nurse's uniform from a hospital that closed a century ago
  layers of shawls and scarves, giving them the silhouette of a pile of laundry given life
  a porter's uniform stiff with starch and something darker at the cuffs
  a wimple and habit, rosary replaced with a string of small teeth
  a chef's whites gone grey, the apron stiff with layers of old meals
  a conductor's cap and tails, the baton replaced with a meat fork
  a haberdasher's apron hung with measuring tapes and shears
  an organist's gown, cathedral-long, trailing black behind
  a gardener's coveralls stained green and brown and one other color
  a postman's uniform, the bag bulging with letters never delivered
  a gravedigger's coat, mud-caked, the pockets heavy with what they've pocketed
  a barkeep's vest and shirtsleeves, one arm stronger than the other from the pulling

clothingMonster
  nothing — their skin IS their garment, and it does not fit
  rags fused into their flesh, grown over and through
  a ceremonial robe split down the back by the growth beneath
  the remnants of a child's clothing, stretched obscenely over a vast frame
  an apron of skin — not their own
  vestments of a faith no one remembers, soaked through and translucent
  a christening gown stretched translucent over a vast, distended torso
  a king's burial shroud, crown fused to the skull beneath
  a wedding dress split up the back by the spine's growth, train dragging like a tongue
  the sodden rags of a drowning victim, perpetually wet, perpetually dripping
  a judge's robes in which they have been encased, the gavel hammered into their palm
  a swarm of small garments — children's clothes — fused into a patchwork hide
  vestments of a high priest, soaked through, the symbols writhing
  a single vast sock, worn like a sheath, the rest of the clothing devoured

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  HAIRSTYLE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
hairstyleKid
  a ragged mop, self-cut with dull scissors
  shaved close — lice, or ritual, or both
  two thin braids tied with dirty string
  a single long strand, the rest fallen out from malnutrition
  hidden entirely under a hood or bag
  wild and uncombed, a bird's nest of tangles
  plastered flat with grease and grime
  a bob, neatly cut — the last relic of a cared-for child
  cropped close on one side, long on the other — they hide behind the long side
  a single topknot, tied with a strip of bedsheet
  hair burnt short on one side where they got too close to a boiler
  a bowl cut, self-inflicted with a kitchen knife, unnervingly even
  covered in a fine layer of dust that will not wash out, making the hair grey
  two pigtails tied with wire, sharp at the ends
  a tonsure shaved by a Resident, for reasons unknown
  hair full of small braids, each tied with a different scavenged thing — a button, a bead, a tooth

hairstyleResident
  a long greasy ponytail, going grey at the root
  bald on top, ringed by a friar's fringe of lank hair
  hair piled high and pinned with rusty needles
  a wig — obviously, badly, a wig
  no hair at all, but a fine down like a moth's wing
  braided so tight it has deformed the skull beneath
  shaved with symbols cut into the scalp
  a tall powdered wig infested with moths, the powder coming off in clouds
  hair lacquered into a single rigid shell, helmet-like, never moving
  a long braid that reaches the floor and is used to tie things
  hair slicked down with something wet and faintly iridescent
  a complex arrangement of pins and rolls, architectural, impermanent
  completely bald but for a single long strand grown to the waist, oiled
  hair that has been set in curlers so long they have grown into the scalp
  a tonsure, monastic, the shaven scalp tattooed with small symbols

hairstyleMonster
  hair that moves on its own, tasting the air
  none — instead, a crown of fused bone
  matted into dreadlocks thick as ropes, swinging like pendulums
  hair grown down to the floor and beyond, used as a sensory net
  a single long strand, impossibly so, trailing behind like a tail
  hair that ignites at the ends without burning, like a candle left too long lit
  no hair, but a surface that ripples like water, suggesting something beneath the skin
  hair grown into the walls around them, rooting them in place, a part of the architecture
  a mane of quills, like a porcupine's, that bristle when they sense prey
  hair that falls upward, defying gravity, drifting toward the ceiling
  thousands of fine tendrils, each ending in a small wet mouth
  a single enormous braid, thick as a limb, that moves on its own
  hair that is actually a colony of small dark insects, parting and closing

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PARTNER / COMPANION
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
partner
  none — they walk alone, as all the small must eventually^2
  a smaller child they found hiding in a pantry, who does not speak
  a mechanical bird that winds itself, whose ticking warns of danger
  a rat with unusual intelligence, who leads them to food and away from traps
  another runaway — they do not trust each other, but they are stronger as two
  a Guest who has retained a sliver of conscience and shields them at great cost
  the ghost of a child who died here long ago, visible only in reflections
  a dog — enormous to them, terrier-sized to the Residents — loyal and afraid
  a shadow that split from their own and now walks beside them
  a music box that, when wound, produces a companion made of sound
  a doll that they are not sure is alive — its head turns when they are not looking
  a sentient puddle of water that reflects things that aren't there and shows the way forward
  a child made entirely of paper, who unfolds to reveal messages and refolds to hide
  a small wind-up nun who blesses them in a tinny voice and frightens the godless things
  a colony of bees that lives in their clothing, loyal to the warmth, deadly to intruders
  a mirror shard that shows whoever last looked into it, and sometimes shows things that have never looked into it
  a singing stone that hums a harmony with the building's groans, masking their footsteps
  a child who exists only in reflections and can move through mirrored surfaces to scout
  a small persistent flame that follows them, neither spreading nor dying, asking nothing
  a knot of rope that has learned to walk and carries them when they are too tired
  the preserved hand of a friend, which points toward safety and away from danger

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  BACKSTORY FRAGMENTS — assembled into a history
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
backstoryOrigin
  arrived as cargo in a crate marked "PERISHABLE"
  wandered in through a door that was not there the day before
  was born here — has never seen the sun, and does not believe in it
  came seeking a sibling who was taken years ago
  washed up on the shore after a storm, half-drowned and hollow-eyed
  was sold by a figure they called Father, for a price paid in teeth
  fell through a rotten floor into a place that should not exist beneath the world
  followed a music box's tune down a staircase that descended for a day and a night
  was left behind by a group that fled — the youngest, the slowest, the forgotten
  climbed aboard what they thought was a ship. It was not a ship.
  was traded for a sack of flour by a mother who was smiling when she did it
  climbed down a well to retrieve a dropped toy and kept climbing down
  was the only one who did not wake up when the others were taken; they woke up here instead
  came in through a painting — stepped into a landscape and the frame closed behind them
  was sent here by a dying grandfather who whispered an address and said "they'll keep you safe"
  walked out of a fog on a road that has no name on any map, and cannot be found again
  was the seventh child of a seventh child, and the debt came due
  arrived in the belly of a fish that washed up on a black sand beach
  came through a door that only opens for those who are lost, and they were very lost
  was left at a crossroads at midnight with a note pinned to their coat that read "PAY WHAT IS OWED"
  followed a procession of moths through a window and down a stair that was not there a moment before
  woke up in a coffin that was not yet nailed shut, in a room full of nailed-shut coffins

backstoryEvent
  once nearly escaped through the kitchens, but was caught by the Cook's shadow
  found a room full of children's shoes and could not stop counting them
  learned to read from the labels on crates, and the labels told a terrible story
  was chosen as a Guest's "favorite" and survived by being entertaining
  discovered that the walls are made of something that was once soft
  saw the Lady combing her hair and was seen in return — has been running since
  made a friend here, once. The friend is now a fixture in the dining hall.
  stole a key from the Janitor's belt and has been hunted for it ever since
  found a mirror that showed a way out, but the way out was through themselves
  was placed on a conveyor belt headed for the grinder, and rolled off just in time
  overheard the Residents singing a lullaby — the words were a recipe
  nursed a broken wing back to flight, and the bird has not left them since
  was almost turned into one of Them, but held onto their name by whispering it hourly
  found a diary written by a child who came before — the last entry was today's date
  once outran a thing with no legs by refusing to look back, and has not looked back since
  found a room where every surface was covered in handprints, all smaller than theirs
  was caught and almost eaten, but escaped by making the Resident laugh — they do not know how
  discovered the pantry is restocked at night, and saw who does the restocking
  learned that the music box tunes are coordinates, and one of them is the way out
  was marked with a symbol by a Resident and has been able to understand the pipes ever since
  found a working telephone that rings once a night, and the voice on the other end knows their name
  nearly drowned in a room that filled with sand in under a minute
  saw their own face among the portraits on the wall, dated a century ago
  was given a gift by a Guest — a small wrapped box they have not yet opened and are afraid to
  found a child's drawing of themselves, sleeping, with a figure standing over them
  once ate the food here and dreamed of the kitchen, and has been hungry in a different way since

backstorySecret
  they are not, strictly, a child — they are what is left of one
  they carry a disease that the Residents fear, though they do not know it
  they have died here before. They do not remember. The place does.
  the key they carry does not open a door — it opens a person
  they are the reason the previous "Guests" never left
  they made a promise to something in the dark, and the dark is collecting
  they are being followed by a version of themselves from a timeline that went worse
  their shadow is not their own — it belonged to the child before them
  they are not running from the place — they are running from what they did to get here
  the key they carry does not open a door — it locks one, and the door must never be locked
  they made a deal: their voice for their life, and the place has been speaking with it ever since
  they are the child of a Resident, and the place is calling them home
  they have been here before, and last time they did something they cannot remember but the walls can
  the smaller child they protect is not real — it is a guilt given form
  they let someone else be taken in their place, and that someone is still down there, waiting
  they are slowly forgetting their own name, and the place is filling the space with its own
  the tears they cry are not theirs — they belong to someone else, someone the place swallowed
  they are the bait. They have always been the bait. They do not know it yet.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  PERSONALITY TRAITS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
trait
  unnervingly calm — smiles at things that should terrify
  fiercely curious, which has saved them and doomed them in equal measure
  quiet to the point of being mistaken for furniture
  prone to sudden, violent resourcefulness when cornered
  kind — dangerously so, in a place that punishes kindness
  suspicious of all comfort, having learned what comfort costs here
  humming constantly, a tune they cannot place — it may be a ward
  obsessively collects small objects: buttons, teeth, coins, keys
  speaks to the walls as though they answer, and perhaps they do
  remembers everything, which is its own kind of torture
  cannot bear to be touched — flinches from all contact
  dreams lucidly and sometimes cannot tell which side of waking they are on
  obsessively tidy — straightens things in rooms that should not be straightened, as if to hold back chaos
  fiercely territorial about small spaces — they will defend a cupboard as if it were a kingdom
  compulsively counts everything — steps, breaths, the eyes of things watching
  unnaturally patient — will wait motionless for hours, which has saved them more than speed ever did
  cruel in small ways to small things, and haunted by each cruelty
  talks to themselves in a second voice, answering, and the second voice knows things they do not
  refuses to sleep in a bed, preferring floors and corners and the undersides of things
  hoards light — matches, candles, fireflies — and will not share it, even when sharing would save a life
  always cold, always shivering, no matter how close to the fire
  keeps a mental tally of everyone who has been kind to them, and repays it in unsettling ways
  cannot lie — the truth comes out of them like a wound, at the worst possible times
  believes they are already dead, and behaves accordingly, which makes them brave and reckless

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  FEAR — what haunts them
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
fear
  the sound of heavy breathing that is not their own
  long fingers — especially when they curl around a door frame
  the dark, but only the kind of dark that moves
  being watched while sleeping
  the smell of cooking meat
  mirrors, and what waits in the fraction of a second before your reflection catches up
  closed doors that open on their own
  the particular silence that means something large has gone still
  being touched while hidden — a finger finding them in the dark
  the number six, for reasons they will not say
  the sound of a clock winding down
  thresholds — the exact moment of crossing from one room to the next
  their own reflection when it moves before they do
  the smell of soap and clean linen
  being underground, which is unfortunate, given where they are
  the sound of a child laughing in the distance
  open doors that reveal only black
  the feeling of being expected — of walking into a room that was prepared for them
  long hallways with a single light at the far end
  the number three, for reasons they counting obsessively to avoid
  the sound of their own heartbeat when everything else is silent
  being forgiven — they do not trust it, and wait for the cost

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  QUIRK — a small, strange detail
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
quirk
  always carries a single hard candy, uneaten, for a friend they hope to find
  counts their steps and will not end on an even number
  sleeps with their eyes open
  hums when frightened — the louder the hum, the greater the fear
  refuses to wear shoes, believing they slow you down when you run
  keeps a list of names of the children who came before, scratched into a spoon
  will not eat anything red
  taps walls three times before passing through any doorway
  collects drops of water on their fingertips and drinks them one by one
  draws eyes on surfaces — chalk, soot, scratched — to watch for them

