// Get all achievement definitions as an array
getAchievements() =>
  let result = [];
  for (let item of achievementData.selectAll) {
    result.push(item.evaluateItem);
  }
  return result;

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  SEASONAL EVENT: THE CONNECTIONS — Launch Celebration
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Event configuration — the event is "always active" in the generator
// since it celebrates the launch. Users can toggle it off.
getEventConfig() =>
  return {
    name: "The Connections",
    subtitle: "Launch Celebration — Limited Time",
    description: "The dark has opened its doors. To celebrate the launch of this generator, the walls remember every connection made here. Special event-themed content is available across all generators — characters who bind, locations that link, encounters that test the ties between souls. These are limited-time additions. The dark is generous today. It will not always be.",
    active: true
  };

// Event-themed characters
eventCharacterName
  The Threadbare Child
  The Bridge Between
  The One Who Remembers Names
  The Knot-Untier
  The First Visitor
  The Echo of Someone You Knew
  The Mirror-Twin
  The Last Link

eventCharacterType
  The Connector — one who binds others together, for weal or for woe
  The Severed — one whose connections have been cut, leaving frayed ends
  The First — the original child, the one who came before all others
  The Bridge — neither here nor there, but the path between

eventCharacterSkill
  can see the invisible threads that bind people together — and cut them
  carries a spool of thread that, when tied between two people, lets them share pain, sight, or breath across any distance
  remembers every name they have ever heard, and speaking a name aloud summons a flicker of that person's presence
  can merge their shadow with another's, becoming invisible as long as that person remains unaware
  their touch leaves a mark — a small knot — that lets them track and find anyone so marked, anywhere in the place
  can speak through the pipes, their voice emerging from any drain or faucet, connecting the separated
  carries a cord woven from the hair of every child they have met; each strand is a connection, and each connection is power
  can trade memories with another, taking their fear and giving their courage, a fair exchange that leaves both changed

eventCharacterClothing
  a coat stitched from patches of other children's clothing, each patch a remembered friend
  a dress woven from thread pulled from every curtain in the place, a patchwork of stolen connections
  rags tied together with dozens of small knots, each knot a promise kept or broken
  a blanket wrapped like a cloak, shared once and never returned, still warm from another's body
  a shirt with dozens of pockets, each containing a small object belonging to someone else
  a veil made from a fishing net, weighted with small tokens — buttons, teeth, keys — each from a different child

eventCharacterBackstory
  was the first child to arrive in this place, long before the others. They remember when the halls were empty, before the Residents came, before the hunger. They have been waiting for connections ever since. The other children do not know them. The walls do.
  once had a sibling — a twin — who was taken to a different part of the place. They have been searching ever since, leaving messages scratched into walls, hoping the twin will find them. The twin has. The twin is not what they were.
  was the one who connected the Residents to each other, weaving a web of alliances and debts. They did this to survive. The web has grown beyond their control. The Residents now move as one mind, and the child is the spider who cannot escape their own web.
  remembers every child who came before. They keep a list — names, descriptions, last known locations. They trade this information. Sometimes for food. Sometimes for company. Sometimes for nothing, just to speak the names aloud and hear them exist in the air.
  was separated from their group during a chase. They found a way to send messages through the pipes — small notes, rolled tight. They have been corresponding with someone on the other end for months. They have never met. They are in love. They are in the same building.
  arrived with a companion who died in the first chapter. They carry the companion's shoe. They talk to it. The shoe, they believe, talks back. The other children have noticed that the child with the shoe always knows things they should not know.

// Event-themed locations
eventLocationName
  The Crossroads of Lost Children
  The Hall of Tied Threads
  The Room Where Hands Meet Through Walls
  The Bridge of Borrowed Faces
  The Gallery of Reflected Selves
  The Pipe Network of Whispers
  The Knot Garden
  The Memorial Wall

eventLocationDesc
  A vast circular chamber where eight corridors meet. At the center stands a pillar covered in names — scratched, painted, bitten into the stone. Children come here to leave their mark, to prove they existed. The pillar hums faintly. It is warmer than it should be. Something in the center is aware of every name.
  Every surface is draped in threads — red, black, white — stretching from wall to wall, floor to ceiling, like a vast loom. Each thread connects two points. Some vibrate. Some are slack. Some have been cut, and the cut ends still twitch. The threads are warm. They pulse. Follow one, and it leads to another room. Follow another, and it leads to a child.
  A long wall, thin enough to see light through it. On both sides, children press their hands flat against the surface. The wall is warm. Hands on the other side press back. You can feel their warmth, their pulse, their fear. You cannot see them. You cannot hear them. But you are not alone, and the wall is the only proof.
  A narrow bridge over an impossibly deep chasm. The bridge is made of faces — pressed flat, frozen, eyes closed or staring. Walking across it, you step on the features of the children who came before. Some of the faces are recent. Some are warm. One of them is smiling at you, and you did not step on it.
  A room of mirrors, but each mirror does not show you — it shows someone else, somewhere else in the place, in real time. You can see them. They can see you. You can communicate through gesture, through expression, through desperate pantomime. The mirrors are cracking, one by one. When a mirror breaks, someone has died.
  A junction in the pipe network where dozens of pipes converge. Sound travels through them — voices, footsteps, breathing. You can hear what is happening in other parts of the place. You can speak into a pipe and be heard. Something else uses the pipes too. It listens. It learns. It repeats.
  A courtyard where the plants grow in knots — spirals, loops, figure-eights. Each knot is a connection between two growing things, woven over years. The gardeners — long gone — were binding the plants together for a reason. The knots are tight. The plants are thriving. The knots are beginning to tighten on their own.
  A long wall at the end of a forgotten corridor. It is covered in messages — scratched, painted, written in substances best not identified. Children have been leaving messages here for as long as the place has existed. Some are warnings. Some are farewells. Some are just names. The most recent one is in your handwriting. You have never been here before.

// Event-themed encounters
eventEncounterType
  The Reunion — two separated characters must find each other across a dangerous space
  The Choice — save the connection or save yourself; you cannot do both
  The Message — a note must be delivered across hostile territory
  The Trust Fall — one character must literally fall, and the other must catch them
  The Shared Dream — two characters experience the same nightmare and must navigate it together
  The Breaking — a bond between two characters is tested to its breaking point
  The Introduction — two strangers meet for the first time in the worst possible circumstances
  The Farewell — one character must leave, and this is the last moment they share

eventEncounterTwist
  the person you are trying to reach is trying to reach you — you are both moving and missing each other
  the message you carry has already been delivered — by someone who came before you, who failed, and whose message was the last thing they did
  the connection you are protecting is not real — it was planted by the place to make you predictable
  the stranger you meet knows your name — and you know theirs — but neither of you has ever met
  the bond breaks not from betrayal but from kindness — one lets the other go, and the letting-go is the wound
  the reunion is a trap — the person you find is wearing the right face but is the wrong thing underneath
  the farewell is permanent in a way neither character understands yet — one of them will not survive the next chapter
  the shared dream reveals that one of the characters is not real — they are a memory the other has been carrying

// Event-exclusive reward
eventReward
  a spool of golden thread — tie it between two characters and they can sense each other's location forever
  a pair of matched buttons — break one and the other shatters wherever it is, a signal across any distance
  a photograph showing two children — one is the protagonist; the other is someone they have not met yet
  a small bell that, when rung, can be heard by every other child in the place — and by everything else
  a handprint pressed into warm wax — placing your hand against it creates a bond with whoever left the original
  a folded paper crane containing a message — the message is from a future version of yourself
  a knot that cannot be untied — it binds two fates together; what happens to one happens to both

// Generate an event-themed character
generateEventCharacter() =>
  let type = eventCharacterType.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let name = eventCharacterName.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let skill = eventCharacterSkill.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let clothing = eventCharacterClothing.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let backstory = eventCharacterBackstory.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let genderVal = gender.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let hairVal = hairstyleKid.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let traitVal = trait.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let fearVal = fear.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let quirkVal = quirk.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  return {
    type: type,
    typeDesc: "A limited-time event character from The Connections celebration. They exist to remind us that even in the dark, nothing is truly alone.",
    name: name,
    gender: genderVal,
    age: "old enough to remember when this place had no other children",
    skill: skill,
    clothing: clothing,
    hair: hairVal,
    partner: "every child they have ever met, carried in memory and in the knots they tie",
    trait: traitVal,
    fear: fearVal,
    quirk: quirkVal,
    history: backstory,
    origin: backstory,
    event: "",
    secret: "",
    event: "The Connections — Launch Celebration"
  };

// Generate an event-themed location
generateEventLocation() =>
  let name = eventLocationName.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let desc = eventLocationDesc.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let danger = locationDanger.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let secret = locationSecret.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  return {
    type: "Event Location — The Connections",
    name: name,
    desc: desc,
    danger: danger,
    secret: secret,
    event: "The Connections — Launch Celebration"
  };

// Generate an event-themed encounter
generateEventEncounter() =>
  let type = eventEncounterType.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let twist = eventEncounterTwist.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let reward = eventReward.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let location = eventLocationName.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let locationDesc = eventLocationDesc.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let complication = encounterComplication.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let atmosphere = encounterAtmosphere.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  return {
    type: type,
    typeDesc: "A limited-time event encounter celebrating the bonds that survive the dark.",
    threat: "Pulse — the connections themselves are in danger",
    scale: "Duo — this encounter is about the space between two souls",
    location: location + " — " + locationDesc,
    atmosphere: atmosphere,
    antagonist: "the distance itself — the dark between two people who need to reach each other",
    objective: type.toLowerCase(),
    twist: twist,
    complication: complication,
    reward: reward,
    rounds: 5 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3),
    event: "The Connections — Launch Celebration"
  };

// Build event character image prompt
buildEventCharacterImagePrompt(char) =>
  let base = "Official Little Nightmares artwork style, 2D dark fantasy concept art, ";
  base += "painterly digital illustration, atmospheric, muted desaturated colors with golden amber accents, ";
  base += "dramatic chiaroscuro lighting, eerie and unsettling mood, detailed texture, Tarsier Studios art style. ";
  base += "Special event character: " + char.type + ". ";
  base += "Named: " + char.name + ". ";
  base += "Appearance: " + char.gender + ", " + char.age + ". ";
  base += "Wearing " + char.clothing + ". ";
  base += "Hair: " + char.hair + ". ";
  base += "The character is surrounded by faint glowing threads connecting them to unseen others, ";
  base += "suggesting invisible bonds and connections. Small fragile figure in a vast ominous environment. ";
  base += "Golden thread motifs woven into the scene, warm and luminous against the dark. ";
  base += "Looming architecture, long shadows, volumetric dust, subtle fog. ";
  base += "Dark background with warm golden light source. ";
  base += toneImageModifier(getCurrentToneLevel());
  base += "Hand-painted concept art aesthetic, celebratory but eerie, no text, no watermark.";
  return base;

// Build event location image prompt
