  let base = "Official Little Nightmares artwork style, 2D dark fantasy environment concept art, ";
  base += "painterly digital illustration, atmospheric, muted desaturated colors with golden amber accents, ";
  base += "dramatic lighting, eerie unsettling mood, Tarsier Studios art style. ";
  base += "Special event location: " + loc.name + ". ";
  base += "Scene: " + loc.desc + " ";
  base += "Golden thread motifs and connection imagery woven into the architecture. ";
  base += "Vast ominous environment with warm golden accents suggesting bonds and links. ";
  base += "Long shadows, volumetric fog, dust particles in golden light beams. ";
  base += "Dark atmospheric background with warm golden light source. ";
  base += toneImageModifier(getCurrentToneLevel());
  base += "Hand-painted concept art aesthetic, no text, no watermark, no characters.";
  return base;

// Build event encounter image prompt
buildEventEncounterImagePrompt(enc) =>
  let base = "Official Little Nightmares artwork style, 2D dark fantasy concept art, ";
  base += "painterly digital illustration, atmospheric, muted desaturated colors with golden amber accents, ";
  base += "dramatic chiaroscuro lighting, eerie and unsettling mood, Tarsier Studios art style. ";
  base += "Special event encounter: " + enc.type + ". ";
  base += "Scene: " + enc.location + " ";
  base += "Atmosphere: " + enc.atmosphere + ". ";
  base += "Two small protagonist figures reaching toward each other across a dangerous space, ";
  base += "connected by a faint golden thread of light. ";
  base += "Vast ominous architecture between them, long shadows, volumetric dust, subtle fog. ";
  base += "Dark background with warm golden light illuminating the space between them. ";
  base += toneImageModifier(getCurrentToneLevel());
  base += "Hand-painted concept art aesthetic, emotional and atmospheric, no text, no watermark.";
  return base;


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  INTERACTIVE MAP GENERATOR — procedural layouts with danger zones
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

mapStyle
  Top-Down Blueprint^2
  Isometric Schematic
  Hand-Drawn Cartography
  Architectural Cross-Section
  Explorer's Sketch

mapRoomName
  The Foyer
  The Vestibule
  The Long Hall
  The Gallery
  The Dining Hall
  The Servants' Passage
  The Pantry
  The Boiler Room
  The Stairwell
  The Landing
  The Library
  The Chapel
  The Nursery
  The Ward
  The Cellar
  The Attic
  The Courtyard
  The Conservatory
  The Ballroom
  The Kitchen
  The Scullery
  The Coal Room
  The Laundry
  The Mailroom
  The Cage Room
  The Sorting Hall
  The Receiving Room
  The Counting House
  The Pipe Junction
  The Mirror Hall
  The Clock Chamber
  The Repository
  The Vestibule of Teeth
  The Wax Room
  The Drawing Room
  The Music Room
  The Map Room
  The Cipher Room
  The Kennel
  The Aviary

mapAnnotationSafe
  This room is quiet — genuinely quiet, not the waiting kind. The door locks from the inside. Breathe here.
  A forgotten corner where the Residents do not patrol. Someone scratched "SAFE" into the wall. It still is.
  The air is still. The shadows are just shadows. Rest if you must, but do not stay long enough to be found.
  A child once made this their hideaway. The blanket is still here. So is the candy they never ate.
  No eyes watch from here. No pipes lead to this room. It is a gap in the place's attention. Use it.
  The dust is undisturbed. Nothing has been here in a long time. Nothing wants to be.
  A warm patch of floor where a pipe runs beneath. It is not a trap. It is just warm. Hold onto that.
  The only room with a window that shows sky — grey, but real. Do not look too long. Do not climb.

mapAnnotationCaution
  The Residents pass through here on a schedule you have not yet learned. Count their steps. Time yours.
  The floor creaks in specific places. You have not mapped which ones. Walk along the walls.
  A Guest dozes in the corner, half-digested meal on their lap. They have not seen you. They wake at sounds.
  The lights flicker here — three seconds on, two off. Move in the dark. Freeze in the light.
  Something scratches behind the wallpaper. It has not broken through. It is patient. So are you. For now.
  The corridor is too narrow to turn around in. If something enters from the far end, you will have to run toward it.
  A trap was here. It has been sprung — by whom, you do not know. The mechanism is spent. The next one will not be.
  The temperature drops sharply. Breath fogs. Something is drawing heat from the room. Find what before it finds you.
  The door sticks. It will take three seconds to open. Three seconds is a long time when something is behind you.
  A Resident's footsteps echo from an adjacent corridor. They are getting louder. They are getting closer.

mapAnnotationDanger
  A Resident sweeps this room with a lantern. The beam is slow but thorough. Stay low. Stay still. Stay invisible.
  The floor is rotten. Weight in the wrong place means a fall into whatever is below. You do not want to know what is below.
  A Guest stands facing the wall, muttering. If they turn, they will see you. They have not turned. Yet.
  The pipes here hiss and vent steam without warning. The steam hides you. The steam also hides what lives in it.
  This room is the hunting ground. Bones are piled in the corner — small ones, many. Move fast. Move now.
  The door behind you has just closed. It does not open from this side. The only way out is forward. Through it.
  Something is breathing in the dark. You cannot see it. It can see you. The exit is twelve steps to your left.
  A mechanism ticks in the walls — blades, perhaps, or crushers. The pattern is irregular. Learn it or be learned.
  The Residents eat here. The table is set. The chairs are occupied. You must cross behind them. Do not breathe.
  A child's voice calls for help from the far corner. It is not a child. It has never been a child. Do not answer.

mapAnnotationLethal
  The Grinder. You can hear it. You can feel the floor vibrate. One wrong step and you are fed into the machine. There is no rescue. There is no remains.
  The floor is alive — a membrane that opens and closes. Time your crossing between its breaths. Miss and you are inside it. Forever.
  The View is here — a vast eye in the ceiling that watches until it finds you, and when it finds you, it does not stop watching, and the room fills with something, and you drown in it.
  The Residents' feeding room. They are here. They are awake. They are looking at the door you just opened. Run is not fast enough. Pray is not enough either.
  This corridor contracts. Slowly, like a throat swallowing. You have forty seconds before the walls meet. The exit is at the far end. It is further than it looks.
  The Bell is here. If it rings — and it rings when the room is disturbed — what comes from below cannot be sent back. Cross without touching anything. Including the floor, if you can manage it.
  The water is black and rising. Something in it is large. Something in it is hungry. Something in it is patient. The exit is across the pool. Swim and be taken. Wait and drown.
  This is where they take the children who are caught. The room is soundproofed. The door is thick. If you enter, you will not leave. If something enters after you, it will.

mapAnnotationFeature
  A chandelier hangs by a single rusted bolt. Cut it and the room goes dark — along with whatever hunts in the light.
  A loose floorboard reveals a cache: three matches, a bent key, and a child's drawing of an exit.
  A mirror on the wall shows the room as it was — not as it is. The reflection includes a door that is no longer there.
  A pipe junction with a valve. Turn it and the steam redirects — clearing one corridor, flooding another.
  A diary page is wedged behind a portrait. It describes the Residents' patrol schedule. It is two days old. It may still be accurate.
  A music box sits on a shelf. Winding it puts the nearest Resident to sleep for ninety seconds. It only works once.
  A crate is half-hidden under a tarp. Inside: a lantern, a rope, and a knife too large for a child to lift.
  A hole in the wall — child-sized — leads to a parallel passage. The passage smells of other children. Old ones.
  A switch on the wall does nothing visible. Elsewhere in the place, a door unlocks. You will not know which one until you find it.
  A set of small footprints in the dust, leading to a vent. The vent is too small for a Resident. It is just right for you.
  A painting has been moved. Behind it: not a safe, but a window into the next room. You can see the danger before you enter it.
  A clock on the wall is running backward. When it strikes midnight — going backward — something in the room changes. You have not waited to see what.
  A bell pull hangs from the ceiling. It is labeled "FOR ASSISTANCE." Pulling it would be a terrible idea. The label is in a child's handwriting.
  A grate in the floor looks down into a lit room below. You can see the exit from here. You can also see what is standing between you and it.

mapSecretFeature
  Behind a loose brick, a child has scratched a map of the ventilation system — every route, every dead end, every exit. It is accurate. It is also annotated: "DON'T TRUST ROOM 7."
  A false wall swings inward to reveal a stair descending. The stair leads to a door. The door leads outside. The way out has been here all along. It has been waiting to be found.
  A loose tile reveals a hollow space containing a key. The key fits a door three rooms back — the one you thought was decorative. It is not decorative. It is the way out.
  Beneath a floorboard, wrapped in oilcloth: a photograph of children playing in sunlight. On the back, a single word: "REMEMBER." Beneath the word, an address. Your address.
  A pipe, when struck three times, opens a panel in the wall. Inside is a flare gun with one charge. It will light the darkest room. It will also alert everything in the building. Choose your moment.
  The mirror in this room does not reflect — it reveals. Looking into it shows the location's secret laid bare: the way out, the danger, the cost. The cost is visible too. You will pay it anyway.
  A child's drawing is pinned behind a painting. It shows an exit through the laundry chute, marked with a crude smiley face. The chute is real. So is what lives in it — but the chute is also the way out, if you are fast enough.
  A loose stone reveals a tunnel — narrow, dark, descending. It bypasses every danger zone in the building. It also bypasses every room. You will arrive at the exit without knowing what you missed. You will always wonder.

getMapAnnotation(zoneType) =>
  if (zoneType === "Safe Haven") return mapAnnotationSafe.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  if (zoneType === "Caution Area") return mapAnnotationCaution.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  if (zoneType === "Danger Zone") return mapAnnotationDanger.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  if (zoneType === "Lethal Zone") return mapAnnotationLethal.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  if (zoneType === "Point of Interest") return mapAnnotationFeature.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  return mapAnnotationCaution.selectOne.evaluateItem;

getZoneColor(zoneType) =>
  if (zoneType === "The Entrance") return "#4a8aaa";
  if (zoneType === "Safe Haven") return "#3a7a4a";
  if (zoneType === "Caution Area") return "#8a7a2a";
  if (zoneType === "Danger Zone") return "#8b4a1a";
  if (zoneType === "Lethal Zone") return "#6a1a1a";
  if (zoneType === "Point of Interest") return "#7a4a8a";
  if (zoneType === "The Secret") return "#8a3a6a";
  if (zoneType === "The Exit") return "#2a7a9a";
  return "#5a5a5a";

// Generate a full procedural map with danger zones
generateMap() =>
  let loc = generateLocation();
  let gridW = 26;
  let gridH = 18;
  let rooms = [];
  let corridors = [];
  let roomId = 0;
  
  let numRooms = 7 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);
  let attempts = 0;
  let usedNames = {};
  
  while (rooms.length < numRooms && attempts < 300) {
    attempts++;
    let rw = 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 4);
    let rh = 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);
    let rx = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * (gridW - rw - 2));
    let ry = 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * (gridH - rh - 2));
    
    let overlaps = false;
    for (let r of rooms) {
      if (rx < r.x + r.w + 1 && rx + rw + 1 > r.x && ry < r.y + r.h + 1 && ry + rh + 1 > r.y) {
        overlaps = true;
        break;
      }
    }
    if (overlaps) continue;
    
    let name;
    let nameAttempts = 0;
    do {
      name = mapRoomName.selectOne.evaluateItem;
      nameAttempts++;
    } while (usedNames[name] && nameAttempts < 20);
    usedNames[name] = true;
    
    rooms.push({
      id: roomId,
      x: rx, y: ry, w: rw, h: rh,
      cx: rx + Math.floor(rw / 2),
      cy: ry + Math.floor(rh / 2),
      name: name,
      zoneType: "",
      annotation: "",
      feature: ""
    });
    roomId++;
  }
  
  if (rooms.length < 3) return generateMap();
  
  let connected = [0];
  let unconnected = [];
  for (let i = 1; i < rooms.length; i++) unconnected.push(i);
  
  while (unconnected.length > 0) {
    let bestDist = Infinity;
    let bestFrom = -1;
    let bestTo = -1;
    for (let fromId of connected) {
      let from = rooms[fromId];
      for (let toId of unconnected) {
        let to = rooms[toId];
        let dx = from.cx - to.cx;
        let dy = from.cy - to.cy;
        let dist = dx * dx + dy * dy;
        if (dist < bestDist) {
          bestDist = dist;
          bestFrom = fromId;
          bestTo = toId;
        }
      }
    }
    if (bestTo === -1) break;
    let from = rooms[bestFrom];
    let to = rooms[bestTo];
    let midX = from.cx;
    let midY = to.cy;
    corridors.push({ x1: from.cx, y1: from.cy, x2: midX, y2: midY });
    corridors.push({ x1: midX, y1: midY, x2: to.cx, y2: to.cy });
    connected.push(bestTo);
    unconnected = unconnected.filter(id => id !== bestTo);
  }
  
  let entranceId = 0;
  let exitId = rooms.length - 1;
  let secretId = -1;
  let available = [];
  for (let r of rooms) {
    if (r.id !== entranceId && r.id !== exitId) available.push(r.id);
  }
  
  for (let i = available.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
    let j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
    let tmp = available[i];
    available[i] = available[j];
    available[j] = tmp;
  }
  
  let assignIdx = 0;
  if (available.length > 0) {
    secretId = available[assignIdx++];
    rooms[secretId].zoneType = "The Secret";
    rooms[secretId].annotation = loc.secret;
    rooms[secretId].feature = mapSecretFeature.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  }
  
  let zonePool = ["Safe Haven", "Caution Area", "Caution Area", "Danger Zone", "Danger Zone", "Lethal Zone", "Point of Interest", "Safe Haven", "Caution Area"];
  for (let i = assignIdx; i < available.length; i++) {
    let zt = zonePool[Math.floor(Math.random() * zonePool.length)];
    rooms[available[i]].zoneType = zt;
    rooms[available[i]].annotation = getMapAnnotation(zt);
    rooms[available[i]].feature = mapAnnotationFeature.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  }
  
  rooms[entranceId].zoneType = "The Entrance";
  rooms[entranceId].annotation = "You entered here. The way back is sealed. The air tastes of copper and beginning.";
  rooms[entranceId].feature = "The door you came through — now a wall. The frame still shows where it was.";
  
  rooms[exitId].zoneType = "The Exit";
  rooms[exitId].annotation = loc.danger;
  rooms[exitId].feature = "The way out. It is watched. It is always watched. " + loc.secret.slice(0, 60) + "...";
  
  let style = mapStyle.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  
  return {
    location: loc,
    rooms: rooms,
    corridors: corridors,
    entrance: entranceId,
    exit: exitId,
    secret: secretId,
    gridW: gridW,
    gridH: gridH,
    style: style
  };

// Build map image prompt — atmospheric cartographic illustration
buildMapImagePrompt(mapData) =>
  let base = toneImageModifier(getCurrentToneLevel());
  base += "Official Little Nightmares artwork style, " + mapData.style + ", ";
  base += "2D dark fantasy environment concept art, atmospheric map illustration, ";
  base += "painterly digital illustration, muted desaturated colors with golden amber accents, ";
  base += "dramatic lighting, eerie unsettling mood, Tarsier Studios art style. ";
  base += "An annotated map of " + mapData.location.name + " — a " + mapData.location.type + ". ";
  base += "The map shows a sprawling layout of rooms and corridors, ";
  base += "with danger zones marked in red, safe areas in green, and a secret area in purple. ";
  base += "Hand-drawn cartographic style with ink and watercolor textures, ";
  base += "aged parchment with stains and tears, cryptic annotations in a child's handwriting. ";
  base += mapData.location.desc + " ";
  base += "Top-down or isometric perspective showing the full layout. ";
  base += "Small figure icons marking points of interest, danger symbols, and a marked exit. ";
  base += "Dark atmospheric border, volumetric dust, subtle fog. ";
  base += "Hand-painted concept art aesthetic, no readable text labels, no watermark.";
  return base;


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  MULTI-CHARACTER SCENE / CAST GENERATOR
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

castSize
  3
  4^2
  5^2
  6

castRole
  The Protagonist^3
  The Antagonist^2
  The Guardian
  The Foil
  The Victim^2
  The Wild Card
  The Mentor
  The Traitor
  The Innocent
  The Survivor
  The Catalyst
  The Doubt

castRoleDesc
  The Protagonist = The child the story follows. Small, determined, afraid. The one who must go forward because going back is no longer an option.
  The Antagonist = The one who rules this place, or serves it, or is it. They do not chase. They do not need to. Their patience is a weapon.
  The Guardian = A figure who shields the protagonist, at great cost. They are not strong enough. They know this. They stand anyway.
  The Foil = A second child whose approach to survival is the mirror-opposite of the protagonist's. Where one hides, the other runs. Where one trusts, the other suspects.
  The Victim = The one who does not make it. Their death — or worse — is the turning point. The protagonist carries the weight of having failed to save them.
  The Wild Card = An unpredictable element — a Resident who wavers, a Guest with a conscience, a child who has gone feral. Their allegiance shifts with the tide.
  The Mentor = An older child, or something that once was one, who teaches the protagonist the rules of the place. The lessons are hard. The teacher is harder.
  The Traitor = A companion who sells the protagonist out, or plans to. The betrayal has not happened yet. It is approaching, patient as the dark.
  The Innocent = A child too young to understand the danger. They must be protected. They cannot be protected. Their presence is the story's heart and its wound.
  The Survivor = A child who has been here longer than anyone. They have seen it all. They have lost it all. They are still here. That is not a comfort.
  The Catalyst = A figure whose arrival or action sets the plot in motion. They may be a Guest, a Resident, or a child. They change everything by walking through a door.
  The Doubt = A presence — perhaps not even a person — that whispers to the protagonist. It questions their resolve, their memories, their name. It is patient. It is persuasive.

castRelationship
  protector and protected — one stands between the other and the dark, at a cost neither has agreed to
  rivals for the same exit — only one can fit through the door, and both know it
  siblings separated by the place and searching for each other across its shifting halls
  strangers bound by circumstance — trust is a currency neither can afford but both must spend
  captive and captor — one holds the key, the other holds the knowledge, and the trade is never fair
  old friends who remember each other differently — the place has edited their shared past
  a debt unpaid — one saved the other's life, and the price of that debt is about to come due
  mirror images — they are alike in ways that disturb, and may be two halves of something that should not have been split
  hunted and hunter — one pursues, one flees, but the roles are not as fixed as they seem
  silent partners — they have never spoken, but they have saved each other three times through action alone
  the betrayer and the betrayed — the wound is old, the forgiveness is new, and neither is certain
  parent and child — the place has warped the relationship, bending it toward something hungrier
  the one who remembers and the one who forgot — between them is the truth of this place, and neither can reach it alone
  the lure and the caught — one was sent to bring the other in. They have decided not to. The place has noticed.

castSceneSetting
  a vast dining hall set for a feast that has just ended — the Guests are slumped in their chairs, and the table is still warm
  a narrow bridge over a chasm with no visible bottom, lit by a single swaying lantern
  a nursery where the toys have rearranged themselves into a circle, and something is sitting in the center of it
  a flooded corridor where the water is black and rising, and the only dry path is a narrow ledge along the wall
  a boiler room where the pipes scream and the floor vibrates, and the only exit is through the furnace
  a mirror maze where the reflections are a half-second behind, and some of them show rooms that do not exist
  a rooftop in the rain where the edge is too close and the wind pushes toward it
  a chapel where the pews are nailed shut and the altar is stained with something that is not wine
  a clocktower mechanism room where the gears are made of bone and the ticking is accelerating
  a laundry room where the washing machines are full of small clothes, still wet, and something is moving behind the dryer
  a cargo hold where the crates are labeled with children's names, and one of the crates is scratching
  a ballroom where a music box plays and the chandeliers sway with no wind, and the dance floor is sticky
  a library where every book is a child's name and a date, and the dates are getting closer to today
  a greenhouse where the plants have learned to move toward warmth, and the characters are warm
  a classroom where the lesson on the board is written in something brown, and the teacher's chair is still warm
  an operating theater where the audience is still seated, still watching, and the stage is set for the next procedure

castSceneMood
  the tension before a betrayal — everyone smiles, everyone waits, no one moves yet
  the aftermath of a loss — the group is smaller now, and the silence is heavier than the screams were
  the moment of discovery — they have found the truth, and the truth is worse than the fear
  the gathering before the descent — they know what lies below, and they go anyway, because the alternative is staying
  the standoff — two of the group want opposite things, and the rest must choose, and the choosing is the horror
  the reunion — someone who was lost has been found, and they are not what they were, and the joy curdles
  the last meal — food has been found, and for a moment they are almost children again, and then the bell rings
  the reckoning — the antagonist is here, in the room, and there is nowhere to go but through
  the quiet before — a rare moment of peace, fragile as held breath, where they tell each other things they have never said
  the breaking point — the group fractures under the weight of the place, and each goes their own way into the dark

castGroupDynamic
  The protagonist leads, the guardian shields, the foil questions every decision — and the traitor watches, patient, from the back.
  They move as a pack, small and fierce, until the first one is taken — and then they are individuals again, scattered, afraid.
  The group is held together by the innocent, the youngest, the one they all protect — and when the innocent is threatened, they become something dangerous.
  The antagonist does not pursue them directly — they send the wild card, who was once a child like the rest, and the group must decide whether to save or to flee.
  The mentor knows the way, but the mentor is changing, becoming something less human, and the group must follow the mentor's map while they still can.
  They are not a team. They are four children in the same corridor, heading the same direction, for different reasons, and the place is testing each reason in turn.
  The victim is the heart of the group — the one who keeps the others human, who shares their food, who sings when the dark gets close. The victim is not going to make it. The group does not know this yet.
  The catalyst arrives mid-journey, a Guest with a conscience or a Resident gone rogue, and their knowledge of the place shifts every calculation the group has made.

// Generate a full cast
generateCast() =>
  let size = parseInt(castSize.selectOne.evaluateItem);
  let location = generateLocation();
  let sceneSetting = castSceneSetting.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let sceneMood = castSceneMood.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let groupDynamic = castGroupDynamic.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  
  let members = [];
  let usedRoles = {};
  let usedNames = {};
  let relationshipPool = [];
  
  for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) {
    let role, roleDesc;
    let attempts = 0;
    do {
      role = castRole.selectOne.evaluateItem;
      attempts++;
    } while (usedRoles[role] && attempts < 30);
    usedRoles[role] = true;
    roleDesc = castRoleDesc[role].evaluateItem;
    
    let char = generateCharacter();
    let nameAttempts = 0;
    while (usedNames[char.name] && nameAttempts < 30) {
      char = generateCharacter();
      nameAttempts++;
    }
    usedNames[char.name] = true;
    
    char.castRole = role;
    char.castRoleDesc = roleDesc;
    members.push(char);
  }
  
  // Assign relationships between pairs
  for (let i = 0; i < members.length; i++) {
    let otherIdx = (i + 1) % members.length;
    if (Math.random() < 0.5 && members.length > 2) {
      otherIdx = (i + 2) % members.length;
    }
    let rel = castRelationship.selectOne.evaluateItem;
    relationshipPool.push({
      a: members[i].name,
      aRole: members[i].castRole,
      b: members[otherIdx].name,
      bRole: members[otherIdx].castRole,
      dynamic: rel
    });
  }
  
  // Deduplicate relationships by pair
  let seen = {};
  let uniqueRels = [];
  for (let r of relationshipPool) {
    let key = [r.a, r.b].sort().join('|');
    if (!seen[key]) {
      seen[key] = true;
      uniqueRels.push(r);
    }
  }
  
  return {
    members: members,
    location: location,
    sceneSetting: sceneSetting,
    sceneMood: sceneMood,
    groupDynamic: groupDynamic,
    relationships: uniqueRels,
    castSize: size
  };

// Build cast image prompt — group scene
buildCastImagePrompt(cast) =>
  let base = toneImageModifier(getCurrentToneLevel());
  base += "Official Little Nightmares artwork style, 2D dark fantasy group scene concept art, ";
  base += "painterly digital illustration, atmospheric, muted desaturated colors with golden amber accents, ";
  base += "dramatic chiaroscuro lighting, eerie and unsettling mood, detailed texture, Tarsier Studios art style. ";
  base += "A group scene with " + cast.castSize + " characters in the Little Nightmares universe. ";
  base += "Setting: " + cast.sceneSetting + ". ";
  base += "Mood: " + cast.sceneMood + ". ";
  base += "Location: " + cast.location.name + " — " + cast.location.type + ". ";
  base += "Characters in the scene: ";
  for (let i = 0; i < cast.members.length; i++) {
    let m = cast.members[i];
    base += m.name + " (a " + m.type.toLowerCase() + ", " + m.gender + ", wearing " + m.clothing + ")";
    if (i < cast.members.length - 1) base += "; ";
  }
  base += ". ";
  base += "The figures are arranged in the scene, their relationships and tensions suggested by body language, proximity, and the direction of their gazes. ";
  base += "Vast ominous architecture dwarfing the figures, long shadows, volumetric dust, subtle fog. ";
  base += "Dark background with a single warm light source illuminating the group. ";
  base += "Hand-painted concept art aesthetic, cinematic multi-character composition, no text, no watermark.";
  return base;

// Build cast text display
buildCastText(cast) =>
  let text = "";
  text += "═══ THE CAST ═══\n";
  text += cast.castSize + " souls bound by the dark\n\n";
  text += "▸ THE SCENE\n" + cast.sceneSetting + "\n";
  text += "Mood: " + cast.sceneMood + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ THE LOCATION\n" + cast.location.name + " (" + cast.location.type + ")\n\n";
  text += "▸ GROUP DYNAMIC\n" + cast.groupDynamic + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ THE CAST\n";
  for (let m of cast.members) {
    text += "  " + m.name + " — " + m.castRole + "\n";
    text += "    " + m.type + " | " + m.gender + " | " + m.skill.slice(0, 50) + "\n";
  }
  text += "\n▸ RELATIONSHIPS\n";
  for (let r of cast.relationships) {
    text += "  " + r.a + " & " + r.b + ": " + r.dynamic + "\n";
  }
  return text;


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CANON RELATIONSHIP GENERATOR — how your OC relates to canon characters
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

canonCharacter
  Six — the girl in the yellow raincoat, small and hungry and surviving the Maw^3
  Mono — the boy with the paper bag, who carries a tuning fork and sees through screens^2
  The Lady — the masked ruler of the Maw, beautiful and terrible, who combs her hair in mirrors^2
  The Janitor (Roger) — the long-armed, blind keeper of the Maw's children, who listens with hands^2
  The Thin Man — the suited figure of the Signal Tower, tall as a doorway, broadcasting dread^2
  The Hunter — the shotgun-wielding hermit of the Wilderness, who hunts small things for sport
  The Teacher — the ruler of the School, whose neck extends impossibly, whose class never graduates
  The Doctor — the obese, crawling physician of the Hospital, who views patients as material
  The Guests — the bloated, gluttonous diners of the Maw, who feast and cannot stop
  The Chefs (The Twin Chefs) — the towering, masked cooks of the Maw's kitchen, who butcher and prepare
  The Granny — the thing in the water beneath the Maw, who pulls swimmers down with long wet fingers
  The Pretender — the child-like doll of the Nest, who mimics innocence to lure the unwary
  The Craftsman — the toymaker of the Nest, old and mechanical, who builds companions from parts
  The Refugee Boy (RK) — a runaway kid in a cardboard box helmet, surviving the streets of the Pale City
  The Flesh Wall — the living, breathing architecture of the Signal Tower, made of flesh and eyes and signal
  The View — the vast eye that opens in the ceiling of certain rooms, watching until it finds you

canonRelationshipType
  hunted by — the canon character actively pursues your OC, for sport, for hunger, or for duty
  allied with — they have formed an uneasy truce, bound by a shared enemy or a shared exit
  mirror of — your OC reflects something the canon character was, or could have been, or fears becoming
  owes a debt to — your OC was saved by the canon character, and the price of that debt is unknown
  descended from — your OC carries something of the canon character within them — blood, curse, or memory
  stalked by — the canon character watches from a distance, patient, curious, preparing something
  former captive of — your OC was once held by the canon character, and escaped — barely
  replaced — your OC has taken the place the canon character once occupied, and the place remembers
  sibling to — they are bound by something deeper than friendship — blood, shared origin, or the place's design
  feared by — the canon character, who frightens everything, is afraid of your OC, and the reason is terrifying
  taught by — the canon character taught your OC the rules of survival, and the lessons left scars
  hunting — your OC is the pursuer, tracking the canon character for revenge, rescue, or something hungrier
  corrupted by — prolonged contact with the canon character has changed your OC, and the change is not complete
  saved by — in a moment of ultimate danger, the canon character intervened — and then was gone
  rivals with — they want the same thing — the exit, the key, the food, the throne — and only one can have it
  parented by — the canon character adopted your OC, in their way, and their way is not gentle
  shadow of — your OC follows in the canon character's wake, seeing what they saw, becoming what they became
  promised to — a bargain was struck, binding your OC to the canon character, and the terms are approaching

canonRelationshipDetail
  The canon character sees your OC as a tool — useful, disposable, and exactly the right size for a very specific purpose.
  They last met in a corridor that no longer exists, and the canon character whispered something your OC has spent every moment since trying to forget.
  The canon character left your OC a gift — a small wrapped box — and your OC has not opened it, and will not say why.
  Your OC knows the canon character's true name, spoken once in the dark, and the name has power that neither fully understands.
  They were separated by a door that closed between them, and the canon character was on the other side, and your OC heard what happened next.
  The canon character tried to eat your OC once. They stopped — not from mercy, but because your OC tasted wrong, in a way that disturbed them.
  Your OC found the canon character's lair, empty, and took something from it. The canon character knows. The canon character is coming.
  They have never met face to face, but your OC has seen the canon character in every mirror in the place, standing just behind them.
  The canon character once protected your OC from something worse, and the protection came with a cost your OC is still paying, installment by installment.
  Your OC reminds the canon character of someone they loved, long ago, before the place took that from them. This makes them gentle. This makes them dangerous.
  The canon character marked your OC — a scar, a symbol, a whisper in the ear — and the mark draws other things to your OC in the dark.
  They made a deal in the boiler room: your OC's freedom for a service not yet named. The canon character is patient. The service will be named.
  Your OC is the reason the canon character is the way they are. They were the first. Your OC was there. Your OC does not remember. The canon character does.
  The canon character believes your OC is the key to their own escape, and they will not let your OC leave — alive or dead — until they are certain.
  Your OC carries a piece of the canon character — a lock of hair, a tooth, a fragment of mask — and the piece is still warm, and it whispers at night.
  The canon character sang your OC to sleep once, in a voice that was almost kind, and the song was a lullaby that means something terrible in a language your OC almost speaks.
  Your OC was the canon character's favorite — the one they kept longest, the one they were gentlest with — and the gentleness was the worst part.
  They are bound by a thread only the canon character can see, and the thread is pulling taut, and something on the other end is reeling it in.

canonRelationshipTwist
  the canon character is not hunting your OC — they are hunting the thing that is hunting your OC, and your OC is the bait
  the relationship has reversed — your OC is becoming the canon character, slowly, and the canon character is becoming something else
  the canon character is dead, and has been for a long time, but the relationship persists because the place does not let debts die
  your OC is not the first to bear this relationship — there have been others, and they are all still here, in the walls, in the water, in the dark
  the canon character is protecting your OC from something they themselves did to your OC, long ago, in a version of events your OC cannot remember
  the bond between them is not natural — it was engineered by the place, and severing it would kill them both
  the canon character has been trying to warn your OC, but the warnings look like attacks, and your OC has been running from the only one who could save them
  your OC is the canon character's replacement — being groomed, slowly, to take their place — and the canon character is doing the grooming
  the debt your OC owes is not to the canon character, but to the thing the canon character used to be, before the place consumed them
  the canon character is afraid of your OC, and has been since the moment they met, and the reason is something your OC has not yet discovered about themselves
  the relationship is a loop — it has happened before, it will happen again, and neither of them remembers the previous times, but the walls do
  your OC carries the canon character's shadow, and the shadow is growing heavier, and one day your OC will set it down, and it will stand up

canonRelationshipOutcome
  your OC escapes the place, but the relationship follows them — in mirrors, in dreams, in the taste of certain foods — and it will never fully let go
  your OC kills the canon character, or the canon character lets themselves be killed, and the act changes your OC in ways that make them the thing they just destroyed
  they part ways at a crossroads — the canon character going deeper, your OC going out — and neither looks back, but both feel the severance like a wound
  the canon character sacrifices themselves so your OC can escape, and the last thing they do is press something into your OC's hand — a key, a name, a promise
  your OC stays behind so the canon character can go free — a reversal of every expected dynamic — and the canon character walks out into a world that does not know what to do with them
  they merge — not metaphorically, but truly — becoming a single entity that is both and neither, and the place accepts this new thing as its own
  the relationship ends not with death or escape but with forgetting — the place takes the memory of each from the other, and they walk separate halls, not knowing what they lost
  your OC inherits the canon character's role, their hunger, their mask, their throne — and the first child to find them will see the canon character's face on a stranger
  they destroy each other, and the place, in a final confrontation, and what remains is a room that smells of ash and two small piles of clothing, one yellow
  the canon character lets your OC go — simply, quietly, opening a door that should not open — and your OC walks through, and the door closes, and neither speaks of it again, and it is the kindest thing the place has ever done

// Generate a canon relationship
generateCanonRelationship() =>
  let char = generateCharacter();
  let canon = canonCharacter.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let canonName = canon.split(' — ')[0];
  let canonDesc = canon.split(' — ')[1] || canon;
  let relType = canonRelationshipType.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let detail = canonRelationshipDetail.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let twist = canonRelationshipTwist.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  let outcome = canonRelationshipOutcome.selectOne.evaluateItem;
  return {
    character: char,
    canonName: canonName,
    canonDesc: canonDesc,
    relationshipType: relType,
    detail: detail,
    twist: twist,
    outcome: outcome
  };

// Build canon relationship image prompt
buildCanonRelationshipImagePrompt(rel) =>
  let base = toneImageModifier(getCurrentToneLevel());
  base += "Official Little Nightmares artwork style, 2D dark fantasy concept art, ";
  base += "painterly digital illustration, atmospheric, muted desaturated colors with golden amber accents, ";
  base += "dramatic chiaroscuro lighting, eerie and unsettling mood, detailed texture, Tarsier Studios art style. ";
  base += "A scene depicting the relationship between two characters in the Little Nightmares universe. ";
  base += "Character 1 (your OC): a " + rel.character.type.toLowerCase() + ", " + rel.character.gender + ", wearing " + rel.character.clothing + ". ";
  base += "Character 2 (canon): " + rel.canonDesc + ". ";
  base += "Relationship: " + rel.relationshipType + ". ";
  base += "The scene shows the dynamic between them — " + rel.detail + " ";
  base += "The two figures are positioned to suggest their bond: hunter and hunted, mirror and reflection, captor and captive. ";
  base += "Vast ominous architecture dwarfing both figures, long shadows, volumetric dust, subtle fog. ";
  base += "Dark background with a single warm light source. ";
  base += "Hand-painted concept art aesthetic, cinematic dual-character composition, no text, no watermark.";
  return base;

// Build canon relationship text
buildCanonRelationshipText(rel) =>
  let text = "";
  text += "═══ " + rel.character.name.toUpperCase() + " & " + rel.canonName.toUpperCase() + " ═══\n\n";
  text += "▸ YOUR OC\n";
  text += rel.character.name + " — a " + rel.character.type + "\n";
  text += rel.character.clothing + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ CANON CHARACTER\n";
  text += rel.canonName + " — " + rel.canonDesc + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ RELATIONSHIP\n";
  text += rel.character.name + " is " + rel.relationshipType + " " + rel.canonName + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ THE BOND\n" + rel.detail + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ THE TWIST\n" + rel.twist + "\n\n";
  text += "▸ THE OUTCOME\n" + rel.outcome + "\n";
  return text;
